@desc Whether the record finds the fact. Refuses, naming the fact, if the record does not say.
GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
      f        IS A `A fact`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the findings` findings `establish` f MEANS
    CONSIDER findings
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the record is silent on` f
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER x
        WHEN `it is the case that` g     THEN IF g EQUALS f THEN TRUE  ELSE `the findings` rest `establish` f
        WHEN `it is not the case that` g THEN IF g EQUALS f THEN FALSE ELSE `the findings` rest `establish` f

@desc Whether the claim's record finds the fact.
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`, f IS A `A fact`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`for` claim `,` f MEANS
    `the findings` (claim's `the findings`) `establish` f

-- A date the record may not hold, read where a rule needs it. Each caller supplies the
-- refusal that names what is missing (phrasebook 11.8: return the refusal, never store it).
GIVEN d IS A MAYBE DATE, missing IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d `, or else` missing MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN JUST x  THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN missing

GIVEN d IS A DATE, a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day` d `falls from` a `to` b `inclusive` MEANS
        d AT LEAST a
    AND d AT MOST  b

-- Every fact the record may find, in the order the nouns declare them: the questions a
-- complete record answers. GENERATED from the enum, like the refusals above.
GIVETH A LIST OF `A fact`
`the facts the record may find` MEANS
